{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C#m]Whom have [A]I but [E]You, oh Lord, to [C#m]carry [E]me through [A]every storm
To [C#m]hold me [E]close and [A]not let go, to [C#m]rescue [E]me in my [A]hour of need
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[E/G#]I proclaim my [A]love
[E/G#]I proclaim my [A]love for You
I will [E]sing it [A]over and [B]over
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[E]Lord on [B]high, You are [A]ever[E]lasting, [B]ever[E]lasting [A]Lord on [B]high
[E]Lord on [B]high, You are [C#m]ever[E]lasting, [A]ever[E]lasting [B]Lord on [E]high
[E]Lord on [B]high, You are [A]ever[E]lasting, [B]ever[E]lasting [A]Lord on [B]high
[E]Lord on [B]high, You are [C#m]ever[E]lasting, [A]ever[E]lasting [B]Lord on [E]high
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C#m]You will [E]lead me and [A]guide my path, [C#m]keeping [E]me on [A]level ground
[C#m]Watching [E]every [A]step I take, [C#m]until I’m [E]in the [A]Promised Land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[E/G#]I proclaim my [A]love
[E/G#]I proclaim my [A]love for You
I will [E]sing it [A]over and [B]over
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[C#m]All the earth declares Your [Bsus/E]glo[E]ry
[C#m]All creation shouts Your [E]praise
Every [A]knee shall bow, every [B]tongue confess
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}
